`)],choices:a,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:n,explanation:["Treat the horizontal and vertical motions separately. The vertical acceleration","$a = F/m$ decides how long each particle takes to reach the landing level. The","horizontal speed then decides how far it travels in that time.","","**Gravitational field:**",...e.gravity,"","**Electric field:**",...e.electric,"","The key difference between the fields: weight is proportional to mass, so every","mass falls with the same acceleration $g$. The electric force $qE$ does not depend on","mass, so in an electric field the acceleration depends on the charge-to-mass ratio $q/m$."].join(`
