`),sampleAnswer:["The problem is that applying classical kinetic energy ($K = \\frac{1}{2}mv^2$)","to find the velocity of each pion gives a value **exceeding $3 \\times 10^8$ m s⁻¹**","(the speed of light), which is impossible according to special relativity.","","This is resolved by applying **special relativity**: at velocities approaching","the speed of light, the relativistic mass of the pion increases, so more energy","is required to further accelerate the pion. Equivalently, using relativistic","momentum $p = \\gamma mv$ and relativistic kinetic energy shows that the pions'","velocity is always less than $c$, with the remaining energy contributing to","the increased relativistic mass rather than further increases in speed."].join(`
