`),marks:2},{question:["Show that the beam has been deflected by about 7.0 mm by the time it","leaves the plates."].join(`
`),sampleAnswer:["Treat the motion like a projectile: the horizontal velocity stays constant","and the vertical motion starts from rest with constant acceleration.","","Time spent between the plates:","$$t_1 = \\frac{6.0 \\times 10^{-3}}{3.0 \\times 10^6}","= 2.0 \\times 10^{-9} \\ \\mathrm{s}$$","","Vertical displacement over that time:","$$s_1 = \\frac{1}{2}at_1^2","= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 3.5 \\times 10^{15} \\times (2.0 \\times 10^{-9})^2","= 7.0 \\times 10^{-3} \\ \\mathrm{m} = 7.0 \\ \\mathrm{mm} \\qquad \\blacksquare$$","","This is less than half the 25 mm gap (12.5 mm), so the beam clears the plates."].join(`
`),marks:2},{question:"Calculate the distance from point P at which the beam strikes the screen.",sampleAnswer:["After leaving the plates there is no field, so the electron moves in a","straight line with the velocity it had at the exit. A common error is to","keep using $\\tfrac{1}{2}at^2$ all the way to the screen.","","Vertical velocity at the exit:","$$v_y = at_1 = 3.5 \\times 10^{15} \\times 2.0 \\times 10^{-9}","= 7.0 \\times 10^6 \\ \\mathrm{m\\ s^{-1}}$$","","Time to cross the 40 mm gap to the screen:","$$t_2 = \\frac{40 \\times 10^{-3}}{3.0 \\times 10^6} \\approx 1.33 \\times 10^{-8} \\ \\mathrm{s}$$","","Extra vertical displacement during the drift:","$$s_2 = v_y t_2 = 7.0 \\times 10^6 \\times 1.33 \\times 10^{-8}","\\approx 9.3 \\times 10^{-2} \\ \\mathrm{m} = 93 \\ \\mathrm{mm}$$","","Total distance from P:","$$d = s_1 + s_2 = 7.0 + 93 \\approx 100 \\ \\mathrm{mm} = 0.10 \\ \\mathrm{m}$$"].join(`
