`),marks:6}}},o1a=[w0a,k0a,S0a,P0a,M0a,N0a,z0a,G0a,K0a,eva,iva,cva,uva,gva],s1a=[wva,kva,Sva,_va,Ova,Rva,Nva,zva,Gva,Xva,Jva,t1a,i1a],r1a=["SE-PF-1"],c1a=["stages of the software development life cycle","levels of testing: unit, integration, system and acceptance","software maintenance and regression testing","Agile sprints and iterative development","comparing waterfall and Agile approaches","the client’s role in acceptance testing"],wK=[{intro:"A team is building a booking app for a dog-grooming business using a sequential (waterfall) approach.",steps:[{text:"Requirements definition",why:"The team first finds out what the business needs the app to do."},{text:"Determining specifications",why:"The needs are turned into precise, testable specifications."},{text:"Design",why:"Algorithms, data structures and screens are planned from the specifications."},{text:"Development",why:"The design is coded."},{text:"Testing and debugging",why:"The finished code is checked against the specifications and errors are fixed."},{text:"Installation",why:"The tested app is deployed for the business to use."},{text:"Maintenance",why:"After release, faults are fixed and changes are made as needs evolve."}],shown:[3,0,6,2,5,1,4],tip:'In a waterfall approach each stage is finished before the next begins, so ask "what must already exist before this step can start?"'},{intro:"A school canteen ordering system is being tested before it goes live. The testing is done in stages, from the smallest parts to the whole system.",steps:[{text:"Unit testing of each function, such as calculating an order total",why:"The smallest pieces are tested on their own first, so faults are easy to locate."},{text:"Integration testing of the menu module working with the payment module",why:"Tested units are combined, and the interfaces between them are checked."},{text:"System testing of the complete system on the school network",why:"The whole system is tested against the specifications in a realistic environment."},{text:"Acceptance testing by canteen staff placing real orders",why:"The client confirms the system meets their requirements before it is signed off."},{text:"Installation for all students and staff",why:"Only an accepted system is released to its users."}],shown:[2,4,0,3,1],tip:"Testing moves outward: a single function, then modules together, then the whole system, then the client."},{intro:"A user of a fitness-tracking app reports that their weekly step total is sometimes wrong. The developers fix the fault during maintenance.",steps:[{text:"Record the user’s fault report",why:"Maintenance begins when a problem is reported and logged."},{text:"Reproduce the fault using the same test data",why:"The developers must see the fault happen before they can investigate it."},{text:"Locate the cause using breakpoints and watches",why:"Debugging tools narrow down which code produces the wrong total."},{text:"Correct the code",why:"The fix can only be written once the cause is known."},{text:"Run regression tests on the existing features",why:"This checks that the fix has not broken anything that used to work."},{text:"Release the update to users",why:"The update ships only after it has passed testing."}],shown:[4,2,5,0,3,1],tip:"A common mistake is releasing straight after correcting the code. Regression testing must come first, because a fix can create new faults."},{intro:"A team uses an Agile approach to build a volunteer roster app for a surf club. Each two-week sprint follows the same cycle.",steps:[{text:"The product owner prioritises the product backlog",why:"The most valuable features must be identified before a sprint is planned."},{text:"Sprint planning selects backlog items for the sprint",why:"The team commits to a small set of the highest-priority items."},{text:"The team develops and tests the items, meeting in daily stand-ups",why:"The work of the sprint happens here, with short daily check-ins."},{text:"Sprint review: the working features are shown to the club",why:"The client sees working software and gives feedback at the end of the sprint."},{text:"Sprint retrospective: the team discusses how to work better",why:"The team reflects on its process last, before the next sprint begins."}],shown:[3,1,4,2,0],tip:"Do not confuse the review with the retrospective: the review looks at the product with the client, while the retrospective looks at the team’s process."}],l1a={id:"software_engineering/Familiarisation/q01",version:1,variants:wK.length,syllabusTopics:[...r1a],learningTopics:c1a,generate(t){const e=wK[t],n=e.shown.map(i=>e.steps[i].text),a=e.steps.map((i,o)=>e.shown.indexOf(o));return{kind:"ordering",question:[e.intro,"","Arrange the steps in the order in which they occur."].join(`
